# What only this site knows about its own files. `alepha build` merges it into
# dist/public/_headers: the security headers helmetOptions produces go above
# it under /*, and a year of immutable caching for every content-hashed file
# (/entry.*, /chunk.*, /asset.*) goes below it. See the deployment guide,
# "Static File Headers".
#
# Every host that serves these files itself applies the merged file:
# Cloudflare (docs deploys through `lore apps deploy`), Bay, and the app's own
# server. Cloudflare defaults every file to
# `cache-control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`, which is right for a
# docs page and is what a file no rule caches gets everywhere.

# Not content-hashed, so not immutable - but a logo that changes twice a year
# has no business being revalidated on every navigation. A day is the honest
# trade between staleness and traffic. A hashed image such as
# `/asset.<hash>.png` also matches these, and the build's hash rules, written
# after them, replace the value rather than join it.
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/*.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# The Bay installer. Anyone sensible reads a script before piping it into a
# root shell, so it is pinned to `text/plain` rather than left to whatever a
# `.sh` extension resolves to - browsers download that instead of showing it.
#
# Deliberately no cache rule: the default `max-age=0, must-revalidate` is
# exactly right for an installer, so a fix to it is picked up on the next run
# rather than a day later.
/bay/install.sh
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
